From: OpenWrt
Subject: net: phy: allow DTS to override LED devicename

Allow PHY LED nodes to specify a custom devicename via the
'linux,led-devicename' property. This is useful when the default
devicename (e.g. "mt7530-0:09") is not user-friendly and a simpler
name like "lan3" is preferred in the sysfs LED class device name.

--- a/drivers/net/phy/phy_device.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/phy_device.c
@@ -3410,8 +3410,11 @@ static int of_phy_led(struct phy_device
 	cdev->max_brightness = 1;
 	init_data.devicename = dev_name(&phydev->mdio.dev);
 	init_data.fwnode = of_fwnode_handle(led);
 	init_data.devname_mandatory = true;
 
+	of_property_read_string(led, "linux,led-devicename",
+				&init_data.devicename);
+
 	err = led_classdev_register_ext(dev, cdev, &init_data);
 	if (err)
 		return err;
